                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/93: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-17T19:00:00+00:00">November 17, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 17—4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1621. I was told at the Foreign Office this afternoon that the report that the
                    Japanese Government had sent some sort of “ultimatum” to the French Government
                    regarding the shipment of munitions through Indo-China to China is entirely
                    untrue. The situation remains that munitions ordered prior to July are permitted
                    to transit Indo-China; the Japanese know this and are displeased; but there has
                    been nothing in the nature of an “ultimatum”.</p>
                <p>Repeated to American delegation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
